# Coding standards

Follow [`docs/coding-standards.md`](docs/coding-standards.md). These enforce our #1 principle: easy-to-read, easy-to-understand code (KISS).

## Must follow

- **Names explain.** Variables/functions read like English and model the business domain.
- **Comments explain why, never what.** Don't restate well-named code.
- **Recipe-shaped code.** Top-to-bottom obvious steps.
- **Functions fit on one screen.** Longer → split into well-named pieces.
- **Lines ≤ 80 characters.** Longer → extract well-named intermediates / simplify.
- **Whitespace groups logical blocks** inside functions.
- **Hate nesting.** Prefer inverted conditions, early returns/guards, then extract functions.
- **Files ~800 lines max.** Over that → split modules by common functionality.
- **No mystery numbers/strings.** Named constants / enum-like maps in domain language.
- **Decompose complex expressions.** Named booleans/intermediates so `if`s read like English.

Clarity beats clever. If two approaches tie, pick the easier read.
